IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-nouns`

-- ind-c-tests-fixtures-g8: the readings of `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` that ind-c's tests hand to the encoding.  Data only, no assertions.
-- Each of the nineteen fork types is distinct, so a reading put in the wrong position is a type error, not a silent swap.

§ `ind-c readings of Articles 26 to 36`

GIVEN f1 IS A `When the retention year of Article 26(5) starts`
      f2 IS A `How promptness under Article 26(6) is judged`
      f3 IS A `Whether Article 28(1)(a) reaches a philosophical belief purpose`
      f4 IS A `Whether the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed`
      f5 IS A `On what ground a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court`
      f6 IS A `From when an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs`
      f7 IS A `How a period fixed by a notice under Article 26 or 27 is counted`
      f8 IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment`
      f9 IS A `Where the retention year of Article 26(5) ends`
      f10 IS A `How a year is added to 29 February under Article 26(5)`
      f11 IS A `Which consents Article 29(1) requires`
      f12 IS A `Whether the first day counts in an appeal time limit under Article 36(2)`
      f13 IS A `Who is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)`
      f14 IS A `What Article 27(1) requires of the Commissioner's belief`
      f15 IS A `Which notices may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`
      f16 IS A `Whether Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration on the charity's own application`
      f17 IS A `When a person must have been a governor to fall within Article 26(2)(b)`
      f18 IS A `How the two grounds of Article 33(5) combine with the two times`
      f19 IS A `Which charity Article 26(4)(a) speaks of`
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
`ind-c G8 reading` f1 f2 f3 f4 f5 f6 f7 f8 f9 f10 f11 f12 f13 f14 f15 f16 f17 f18 f19 MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` WITH
        `when the retention year of Article 26(5) starts` IS f1
        `how promptness under Article 26(6) is judged` IS f2
        `whether Article 28(1)(a) reaches a philosophical belief purpose` IS f3
        `whether the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed` IS f4
        `on what ground a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court` IS f5
        `from when an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs` IS f6
        `how a period fixed by a notice under Article 26 or 27 is counted` IS f7
        `unit of the terms of imprisonment in Articles 26 and 29` IS f8
        `where the retention year of Article 26(5) ends` IS f9
        `how a year is added to 29 February under Article 26(5)` IS f10
        `which consents Article 29(1) requires` IS f11
        `whether the first day counts in an appeal time limit under Article 36(2)` IS f12
        `who is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)` IS f13
        `what Article 27(1) requires of the Commissioner's belief` IS f14
        `which notices may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS f15
        `whether Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration on the charity's own application` IS f16
        `when a person must have been a governor to fall within Article 26(2)(b)` IS f17
        `how the two grounds of Article 33(5) combine with the two times` IS f18
        `which charity Article 26(4)(a) speaks of` IS f19

-- The reading the encoding takes at every fork (each field's TYPICALLY).
`ind-c G8 A` MEANS
    `ind-c G8 reading`
        `the year of Article 26(5) runs from the day the document is provided or retained`
        `promptness under Article 26(6) is a judgement the caller supplies`
        `only a purpose within Article 6(1)(c) counts under Article 28(1)(a)`
        `the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed`
        `a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court only on the ground in Article 35(1)`
        `an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs from the notice of the decision`
        `the day of service is not counted in a period fixed by a notice`
        `calendar months`
        `the year of Article 26(5) ends on the anniversary of the day it starts`
        `a year of Article 26(5) from 29 February ends on 28 February`
        `Article 29(1) requires both consents`
        `the day of the anchor is not counted in an appeal time limit`
        `any applicant for registration or registered charity is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)`
        `the Commissioner's belief alone is the ground under Article 27(1)`
        `only a notice under Article 27(1)(c) or (d) may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`
        `Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration granted on the charity's own application`
        `a governor at any time of an entity registered at any time falls within Article 26(2)(b)`
        `each ground of Article 33(5) must hold at both times`
        `the registered charity of Article 26(4)(a) is a charity registered now`

-- One record per other reading, each differing from `ind-c G8 A` at that fork alone.
